==============================================================================
 CV(H)^2 over labeled tournaments -- exact even-run closed form (klein-S5)
==============================================================================
 cross-checks (perm form vs even-run DP vs direct tournament enumeration):
    n     A_perm  A_evenrun    CV^2 (frac)      CV^2   n*CV^2
    2          2          2              0   0.00000   0.0000  direct=OK
    3          8          8            1/3   0.33333   1.0000  direct=OK
    4         32         32            1/3   0.33333   1.3333  direct=OK
    5        158        158          19/60   0.31667   1.5833  direct=OK
    6        928        928          13/45   0.28889   1.7333
    7       6350       6350        131/504   0.25992   1.8194
    8      49752      49752        131/560   0.23393   1.8714
    9     439670     439670      1097/5184   0.21161   1.9045

 A_n(2) sequence (for OEIS): [1, 2, 8, 32, 158, 928, 6350, 49752, 439670, 4327904, 46963358]

 n*CV(H)^2 -> 2  (the dominant fluctuation is a single length-2 overlap run):
   n=  10:  CV^2 = 0.192654   n*CV^2 = 1.92654
   n=  20:  CV^2 = 0.099274   n*CV^2 = 1.98548
   n=  40:  CV^2 = 0.049919   n*CV^2 = 1.99676
   n=  80:  CV^2 = 0.024990   n*CV^2 = 1.99923
   n= 160:  CV^2 = 0.012499   n*CV^2 = 1.99981
   n= 320:  CV^2 = 0.006250   n*CV^2 = 1.99995

 => CV(H)^2 ~ 2/n exactly: H concentrates, std/mean ~ sqrt(2/n). The even-run parity
    (odd overlap runs cancel) is the S_n-side mirror of the LRC 2-adic descent (THM-580).
